  "name": "Question 17",
  "problem": "A parcel delivery company records whether each delivered package requires a signature upon arrival. On average, $9$ out of $50$ packages require a signature. Each package's status is independent of the others. Rounded to $3$ decimal places, the probability that the first package requiring a signature is the fifth package delivered or later is{{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "A geometric random variable $X$ with probability of success $p$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(1-p)^{x-1}p\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the number of packages delivered until a package that requires a signature is delivered. On average, the chance that any single package requires a signature is \n\n$$\np=\\frac{9}{50}=0.18.\n$$\n\nSo, the number of packages until the first package that requires a signature is delivered can be modeled as a geometric random variable with a probability of success $p=0.18.$\n\nSo, $X\u223c\\text{Geom}(0.18).$ In this case, $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={(1-0.18)}^{x-1}(0.18) \\\\  & ={(0.82)}^{x-1}(0.18)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo compute $P(X\\ge 5),$ we will use the complement:\n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 5)=1-P(X<5)\n$$\n\nComputing the probability of the complement, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<5) & =P(X\\in {1,2,3,4}) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3)+f(4) \\\\  & =(0.82)^{1-1}(0.18)+(0.82)^{2-1}(0.18)+(0.82)^{3-1}(0.18)+(0.82)^{4-1}(0.18) \\\\  & =(0.18)+(0.82)(0.18)+(0.82)^{2}(0.18)+(0.82)^{3}(0.18) \\\\  & =[1+0.82+(0.82)^{2}+(0.82)^{3}](0.18) \\\\  & \u22480.548,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\nTherefore, the probability that at least $4$ packages are delivered before the first package that requires a signature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 5) & =1-P(X<5) \\\\  & \u22481-0.548 \\\\  & \u22480.452,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
